<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jeddah</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jidda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jeddah is a port city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a> in Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>. Made the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> Uthman in the 7th century, it became the main gateway for pilgrims arriving by sea and a centre of Red Sea trade. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Ibn Saud</a> took it in 1925, and it served as Saudi Arabia's diplomatic capital and remains its chief commercial city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jeddah.jpg" alt="Jeddah" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jeddah_Waterfront,_Western_Saudi_Arabia_(2026).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
